{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>You shall not hate your brother.</b> The opposite of \"and you shall love your neighbor.\" Now, all these commandments are planted in the heart, and by their observance they shall dwell in the land, for on account of baseless hatred the Second Temple was destroyed." "<b>You shall surely reprove.</b> Perhaps you will suspect him of something and it is not so, and this is the meaning of \"and you shall not bear sin on his account,\" for there will be punishment upon you on his account."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:10:57.276938884Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}